cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Dark Mode System Default Checker
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Aesthetic Vulpes
    website: https://github.com/didvc/
repository-code: https://github.com/html-js/dark-mode-system-default-checker
url: https://html-js.github.io/dark-mode-system-default-checker/
license: AGPL-3.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
abstract: >
  A single-page, zero-dependency browser tool that reports whether the
  browser asks websites for a light or dark color scheme and which layer
  decided it. It reads prefers-color-scheme and related media features live,
  resolves CSS system colors per color-scheme, flags forced colors, contrast
  and inversion settings, detects page restyling by add-ons, and offers a
  visual self-test for automatic force-dark modes. Everything runs locally.
keywords:
  - dark-mode
  - light-mode
  - prefers-color-scheme
  - color-scheme
  - forced-colors
  - prefers-contrast
  - system-colors
  - auto-dark-mode
  - accessibility
  - web-development
